# Throw a Javelin of Lightning at a visible creature and read the Reflex-save
# DC that the player is shown (PA-08-F47 of bd inc-tek.8.8).
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. Creature::SavingThrow prints the subject's Reflex
# roll as "1d20 ... vs DC D" when the player perceives it. With Store Rolls in
# Log enabled, the same player-facing line is retained in the message log and
# photographed by the savedc-log dump below. D must be 10 + half the thrower's
# total character level + the thrower's Dexterity modifier, as the item's Desc
# promises. The character sheet dump records both inputs.
#
# ON A BUILD WITHOUT THE FIX the weapon effect leaves saveDC non-positive.
# SavingThrow returns before printing a roll, so savedc-log contains no
# javelin-generated "Reflex Save" / "vs DC" line and the subject takes full
# damage. With the fix, that line appears with the computed DC.
#
# WHY A GOBLIN AND WHY FREEZE IT. A plain goblin has no electricity resistance
# or immunity and is visible to the adjacent player, so the SavingThrow show
# branch runs. Freeze Monsters keeps it one square east without suppressing a
# saving throw caused by the player's attack. Free Advancement makes the
# barbarian level 3, giving the half-level term a visible value of 1.
#
# Menu letters and generated attributes depend on the seed. Run at seed 1 with
# INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat; that pinned file keeps Store Rolls
# in Log enabled.

@include chargen.keys
@until "Afoot" ESC

# Free Advancement (third row) and Freeze Monsters (eleventh row).
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*2
SPACE
DOWN*8
SPACE
ESC

# Raise the barbarian from level 1 to level 3, then record level and Dexterity.
d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel hardier" ESC
@expect "Barbarian 3"
@dump:thrower-sheet
ESC

# Put the named specific weapon in the weapon hand.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10
@until "Javelin of Lightning" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
2
ENTER
b
SPACE
s
@dump:javelin-ready
ESC

# A visible, non-electric-resistant subject, frozen one square east.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:subject-ready

# Fire Ranged Weapon: choose the javelin, then target the adjacent goblin.
f
a
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:after-throw

# Store Rolls in Log makes the save line persist here after the effect resolves.
v
@dump:savedc-log
ESC
@quit
